From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kefu Chai <k.chai@proxmox.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:34:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mon/AuthMonitor: link the PVE cephx migration docs in
 insecure key warnings

Ceph 19.2.6 and 20.2.4 added health checks for keys, service tickets
and cipher settings that still use aes, so PVE users can see them right
after a point release upgrade without knowing what to do next. The
migration has to be done with the pve-cephx-rotate-service-keys helper,
which also updates the key copies managed by PVE, instead of the
upstream procedure.

The web interface explains each of these checks and links the guide
next to them, but somebody reading "ceph -s" or "ceph health" over ssh
gets the summary and nothing else, so the summary has to carry the
link.

Only AUTH_INSECURE_KEYS_ALLOWED carries it. That check is raised for as
long as the monitors still allow aes, and the documented procedure
restricts the allowed ciphers in its last step and only through the
helper, so the check tracks whether the migration is finished. The
others clear earlier: the two error severity ones go away in step 1,
the rotating service key warning expires by itself, and the last two
are the ones the PVE docs tell users to mute while an incompatible
client keeps the migration from finishing. Linking those as well would
repeat the same url up to six times in one "ceph health" line and in
the cluster log.

The summary points at the PVE documentation, so this change is not
meant for upstream. It lives in the Proxmox patch series.

Signed-off-by: Kefu Chai <k.chai@proxmox.com>
---
 src/mon/AuthMonitor.cc | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mon/AuthMonitor.cc b/src/mon/AuthMonitor.cc
index 00d3fe99344..434470c537b 100644
--- a/src/mon/AuthMonitor.cc
+++ b/src/mon/AuthMonitor.cc
@@ -498,7 +498,10 @@ bool AuthMonitor::check_health()
       }
     }
     if (!details.empty()) {
-      auto& check = next.add("AUTH_INSECURE_KEYS_ALLOWED", HEALTH_WARN, "Monitors are configured to allow auth using insecure key types", details.size());
+      auto& check = next.add("AUTH_INSECURE_KEYS_ALLOWED", HEALTH_WARN,
+                             "Monitors are configured to allow auth using insecure key types"
+                             ", see https://pve.proxmox.com/pve-docs/chapter-pveceph.html#pveceph_cephx_migration",
+                             details.size());
       for (auto& detail : details) {
         check.detail.push_back(detail);
       }
